        "project_name": "Channel Mission Bay",
        "site": "Mission Bay South",
        "status": "complete",
        "use": "residential",
        "geometry_type": "real",
        "digitized_from": "DataSF Assessor parcels (acdm-wktn), lots 8711023B and 8711023C (mapped 2021-06-02; active), joined into one outline; the earlier outline came from: DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF8711023); name/address from OpenStreetMap way 1208613094 (185 Channel St)",
        "digitization_method": "ADDED 2026-09-19 for Mission Bay's third real-buildings pass (remaining uncovered footprints inside the official Mission Bay North/South redevelopment-area boundary): Channel Mission Bay, a 315-unit apartment building at 185 Channel St, developed by DOB Mission Bay LP with design/development by LaHue and Associates, managed by UDR. 2026-09-29 accuracy audit: none of the three geo sources cited above gives a unit count; 315 units is from DBI permit #201104224606 ('to erect 8 stories, 315 units residential, retail, parking building', via DataSF i98e-djp9), while the Assessor's 2015 roll records 316 units. 2026-10-02: public-text pass. accuracy_caveat, notes reworded for readers (meaning unchanged; no change to the shape, status, use or geometry_type); previous wording -- accuracy_caveat: 'REAL -- surveyed DataSF Building Footprints outline (mblr SF8711023), cross-referenced by position against an OpenStreetMap building/address point (way 1208613094) for the name and street address; not a hand trace or plan estimate. Opening year not confirmed by any source found in this pass.'; notes: 'Opening year not confirmed by any source found in this pass.'. REPLACED 2026-10-12 (shape; status and use unchanged): the owner approved building records whose outline matches an Assessor lot at 85% or better, both ways, using the lot (CLAUDE.md, 'An official parcel beats our drawing'). DataSF's Assessor layer (data/raw/parcels.geojson) has the union of Assessor lots 8711023B and 8711023C (8,375 m2, active, mapped 2021-06-02); the earlier outline of 6,361 m2 and the lot overlap with IoU 0.71 (96% of the earlier outline lies inside the lot and it covers 73% of the lot). The outline is now their union using the lots' own vertices (no simplification). geometry_type stays 'real'. Previous digitized_from: 'DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF8711023); name/address from OpenStreetMap way 1208613094 (185 Channel St)'. Previous accuracy_caveat: 'REAL -- surveyed DataSF Building Footprints outline (mblr SF8711023), cross-referenced by position against an OpenStreetMap building/address point (way 1208613094) for the name and street address; not a hand trace or plan estimate. Opening year not confirmed by any source found.'.",
        "accuracy_caveat": "REAL lot geometry -- the outline is the union of Assessor lots 8711023B and 8711023C (8,375 m2, active), so its edges are recorded lot lines, not a surveyed building footprint: it includes any yard, setback or plaza inside the lot and can sit a little off the walls. Until 2026-10-12 this record showed the surveyed building footprint (DataSF Building Footprints (mblr SF8711023)); 96% of that outline lies inside the lot and it covered 73% of the lot.",
        "notes": "Opening year not confirmed by any source found.",
